## Grafana Agent Observability gains OpenTelemetry support

Source: Grafana Labs — https://grafana.com/press/2026/10/20/observabilitycon-2026-ai-updates/
Published: 2026-10-20
Channel: news

Grafana Labs announced general availability of OpenTelemetry support for Agent Observability at ObservabilityCON. The release targets visibility into production-agent behavior and cost without requiring teams to introduce a separate monitoring product.

The announcement also makes Assistant Watchers generally available. Teams describe what matters in natural language; Watchers learn patterns from their telemetry and report changes with supporting evidence through Grafana Alerting. Critical findings can initiate a deeper Investigation. Grafana describes Watchers as a complement to threshold alerts, not a replacement.

Two related capabilities remain public previews. Managed Sandboxes provide a cloud environment where Assistant can inspect repository code against production telemetry, propose a fix, and open a pull request for human review. Grafana Pages extend visualization beyond conventional dashboards. These are vendor announcements rather than independent tests of diagnosis accuracy or safe remediation. For operators, the important distinction is between observing an application’s agents and authorizing an agent to change that application.

Why it matters: Keep instrumentation coverage separate from remediation permissions.

