## Cisco survey connects agent oversight with clearer operational ownership

Source: Cisco — https://blogs.cisco.com/news/state-of-observability-2026-reveals-how-leaders-are-restoring-predictability-to-the-agentic-era
Published: 2026-10-20
Channel: news

Cisco’s State of Observability 2026 report draws on responses from 2,050 ITOps and engineering professionals across ten countries and sixteen industries. Its central concern is that agents can change execution paths without a corresponding application deployment.

The publisher reports that 83% of respondents worry about unintended consequences from AI agents. Among its designated leader cohort, 91% report clearly defined ownership and accountability for monitoring AI, compared with 59% of other respondents. Leaders also report more monitoring complexity, suggesting that broader visibility does not necessarily make the underlying workload simpler.

Cost findings complicate the assumption that AI infrastructure dominates observability spending: only 6% named it their largest cost driver, while excessively verbose logging led the list. Cisco argues for deliberate sampling, routing and connecting telemetry to business decisions. These results are self-reported survey associations, not controlled evidence that a particular product or governance practice causes better outcomes. Use the findings as questions for an operational review, not product-selection evidence.

Why it matters: Assign owners for agent behavior and telemetry budgets.

